														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2301620">
									

<p>Ok, so&#8230;</p>
<p>It's very similar to <a href="/scp-869">SCP-869</a> in terms of initial conception, containment procedures, and New York-iness (Although if it's not on Coney Island, it's probably New Jersey-ness, and I sincerely apologize for the implication.)</p>
<p>The other world is fairly similar to <a href="/scp-1165">SCP-1165</a> (among others, I think) in the boundaried back-of-the-world idea.</p>
<p>I don't mind the redaction listed above. It's not perfect redaction, but it does leave me room in my head to play around with what happens with people who stayed there, which is a big part of the fun of both 869 and being in a weird semi-Earthly other dimension.</p>
<p>Ultimately, I do like this. It's well put together and the interview log is good, even if the twist it adds is&#8230; not bland or overdone, but a little basic.</p>
<p>I just don't know if it stands out enough from things on the site. No vote for just now. I'll give it another read when I've had more sleep, see if I have a more solid impression.</p>
<p>EDIT: Also, <a href="/scp-2727">SCP-2727</a>, which, while narratively/tonally different, has a huge amount of stylistic overlap.</p>

